    <h2>Common Situations We Handle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Planning an extended stay in the Philippines</li>
      <li>Retirement or long-term relocation</li>
      <li>Family reunification on a long-term basis</li>
      <li>Investment-linked or other long-term status pathways</li>
      <li>Other residency-related circumstances</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Retiring in the Philippines</h2>
    <p>Foreign nationals retiring in the Philippines typically do so through the Special Resident Retiree's Visa (SRRV), a programme administered by the Philippine Retirement Authority (PRA) rather than the Bureau of Immigration directly. We assist with the immigration-side coordination of an SRRV application and the documentation surrounding it, working alongside the PRA's own process.</p>

    <h2>Bringing Your Family</h2>
    <p>Long-term status is often a family decision as much as an individual one. If you're relocating with a spouse, partner or dependants, see our <a href="/services/family-and-spousal-visas/">Family &amp; Spousal Visas</a> service alongside this one.</p>

    <h2>How the Process Works</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li>
        <h3>Initial enquiry</h3>
        <p>Tell us about your long-term plans for the Philippines.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Assessment</h3>
        <p>We review your circumstances and explain which options may be available to you.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Preparation</h3>
        <p>We help you prepare and organise the required documentation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Submission and follow-up</h3>
        <p>We manage your application and keep you informed of its progress.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What We May Need From You</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your passport and current immigration status</li>
      <li>Details of your long-term plans and circumstances</li>
      <li>Supporting documentation relevant to the specific pathway, such as financial, family or investment documentation, where applicable</li>
    </ul>

